{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098981-winterberry-a-setting-idea-seeking-advice","id":1098981,"title":"Winterberry. A setting idea. Seeking advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T19:16:11-07:00","id":1098981,"title":"Winterberry. A setting idea. Seeking advice","content":"I am thinking about buying C20 when it comes out and I have been brainstorming a setting for it. The setting is a small town in Maine called Winterberry. It was founded in the 1700s as a whaling community and has always had the charm that some sea-side villages have. The town has always strived to appear wholesome in order to attract new residents. Because of this, instead of demolishing old historic buildings, the town renovates them and turns them into either museums or makes them bed and breakfasts. The town also has the same pier that was built in the 1700s,but heavily renovated and repaired to keep it from rotting away. What the town doesn't know is that within their community is a minority population of Changelings. They came to the town with the original citizens but stayed due to the glamour the little costal village seemed to generate.<br /> <br /> Helping the towns glamour is the urban legend that surrounds it. During the 1920s, the town was used by bootleggers to smuggle rum into the country. The most infamous of these gangsters was No-Neck Bill. Bill, who was public enemy number five by the time Prohibition ended, had made himself quite a fortune in the smuggling game. In 1935, Bill realized that the Feds were after him and he decided to split. Before he left however, he stashed over 10,000 dollars in a satchel in hid it somewhere in the towns many costal caves, intending on coming back for it later. But, Bill never returned and his hidden cash hoard had become one of the many urban legends that surround the town. Bill's loot has also contributed to the town's lucrative tourist trade as people come to the town from around the world in hopes of snagging Bill's loot for themselves.<br /> <br /> \u200bDespite the towns innocent looking exterior, it has been having a crime problem as of late. The reasoning for this is that their are two rival street gangs inhabiting the town. These gangs are the 9th Avenue Skulls and the Winterberry Overlords. These two gangs have been at each others throats as of late and it is rumored amongst the Changeling community that the leader of the Overlords is actually a Unseelie Changeling, though which kith is unknown. The towns crime problems have also been caused by Lucas Stringali, a mafia capo that is running a chop shop racket from a auto shop in downtown.<br /> <br /> The year is 1984 and the town is celebrating it's bi-centennial. You are changelings living within the town. As Changelings, the opportunities the town presents to get glamour is almost endless. You can find No-Neck Bills' treasure, explore the many caves along the coast, find old colonial artifacts and possibly explore shipwrecks. But, make sure to watch out for the Overlords and the Skulls.<br /> <br /> \u200bI need help detailing the changeling community within Winterberry and detailing the Dreaming version of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:38:39-07:00","id":1098994,"title":"","content":"Redcap rum-runners sounds <i>awesome</i>, so maybe No-Neck Bill was a redcap and his reincarnation has come to town to find his cash. Problem is---<i>he can't remember where he put it</i>. To kill time, he founded the Winterberry Overlords. Old habits, and all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}